  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With the new trust and safety system, avatar creators, especially those who have popular avatar worlds, will be looking to use shaders that are whitelisted by default so that players can see the avatar displayed with the correct shading, regardless of user rank.\n\nThere seems to be a small, undocumented assortment of shaders that are currently whitelisted - certain versions of CubedParadox's Flat Lit seem to work while others don't, as an example. (I did not spend long testing or figuring the whitelist out for myself yet)\n\nIt would be nice to have an idea of what creators can use that VRChat will display by default.",
